---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About The Grounded Elephant"
  description="Who made Groundwork, why it exists, and how it is kept honest.">

  <section class="about">
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Hi. My name is Miranda.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I am a social work student, finishing my BSW and heading into my MSW. Groundwork was born because I was
      sick of searching all over the internet for everything we need in this work. So let's lay the groundwork
      for your career.
    </p>

    <h2>It started as my own cheat sheet</h2>
    <p>
      Practicum at a domestic violence shelter in the Texas Hill Country, a stack of half-remembered theories,
      and a resource list that lived in six browser tabs and a photo of a binder page. I built the thing I wished
      someone had handed me. Then other students and clinicians wanted it, so here it is.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      A working reference, not a textbook. The theories under the work, the modalities used in session, screeners
      you can score on the spot, group plans you can run this week, printable handouts, licensing and
      supervision rules for Texas, California, Florida, Washington, New York, Pennsylvania, and Illinois, a filterable resource directory, and a shelter list with phone numbers that actually
      connect. Built for the moment you need the answer, not the semester you learn it.
    </p>

    <h2>What it isn't</h2>
    <p>
      Groundwork does not replace supervision, your agency's policies, your own clinical judgment, or your state
      licensing board. If something here and your supervisor disagree, your supervisor wins. If something here and
      the law disagree, the law wins, and I want to hear about it.
    </p>

    <h2>How it stays honest</h2>
    <p>
      Every rule is quoted from the actual rulebook or statute and cited by number. Every fee, hour count, and
      phone number was verified against the primary source before it went in, and the date of the last check sits
      in the footer. Anything that only applies in one state is badged with that state, <strong>Texas</strong>, <strong>California</strong>,
      <strong>Florida</strong>, <strong>Washington</strong>, <strong>New York</strong>, <strong>Pennsylvania</strong>, or <strong>Illinois</strong>, and anything that applies everywhere is badged <strong>National</strong>,
      so nobody gets caught by a rule that isn't theirs.
    </p>

    <div class="why">
      <div>
        <h2>Why an elephant</h2>
        <p>Elephants remember everything and never leave the herd behind. That felt about right.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="contact">Send me your requests</h2>
    <p>
      Groundwork gets better every time someone tells me what is missing. A resource that closed, a fee that changed,
      a rule that got amended, a worksheet you wish existed, a section you want added. Send it over and I will
      look into it.
    </p>
    <p class="contact-row">
      <a class="btn btn-mail" href="mailto:groundedelephant@gmail.com?subject=Groundwork%20request">groundedelephant@gmail.com</a>
    </p>

    <h2 id="privacy">Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Groundwork collects nothing about you. There are no accounts, no analytics, no advertising, and no cookies.
      The only things stored are your chosen state and your light or dark setting, and those live in your own
      browser so the site can remember them next time; clearing your browser data removes them. Nothing you print
      or type into a printout leaves your device. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, whose servers keep the
      ordinary logs any web host keeps; GitHub's own privacy statement covers those. Links to other sites take you
      to those sites, with their own rules.
    </p>

    <p class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#start">Lay the Groundwork</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .kicker{font-size:0.72rem; font-weight:700; letter-spacing:0.1em; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--wine); margin:0 0 8px;}
  .about{max-width:76ch;}
  .about h1{font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:clamp(1.9rem,4vw,2.6rem); line-height:1.15; margin:0 0 12px;}
  .about h2{font-family:var(--font-display); font-size:1.25rem; margin:30px 0 8px;}
  .lede{font-size:1.1rem; color:var(--ink-soft); margin:0 0 6px;}
  .about p{margin:0 0 12px;}
  .cta{margin-top:28px;}
  .why{display:flex; gap:28px; align-items:flex-start; flex-wrap:wrap;}
  .why > div{flex:1 1 260px;}
  .spray-fig{flex:0 1 320px; margin:6px 0 0;}
  .spray-fig figcaption{font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--ink-soft); margin-top:6px; text-align:center;}
  .contact-row{margin:6px 0 0;}
  .btn{display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; text-decoration:none; font-weight:600; font-size:0.92rem; padding:11px 18px; border-radius:99px;
       border:1px solid var(--pine); color:var(--on-accent); background:var(--pine); box-shadow:var(--shadow);}
  .btn-mail{background:var(--paper-raised); color:var(--pine); border-color:var(--pine);}
</style>
